## Never hand-edit in the wiki

A session changes these wiki paths only through the kit CLIs (the event
CLI for events and corrections, the renderers for projections, the
doctor to check). The wiki's pre-commit hook rejects most direct edits at
commit time and the wiki's own Claude Code settings deny its edit tools;
nothing stops a shell write or another harness, so this list is the
rule, not the mechanism:

{{PROTECTED_PATHS}}

What each path is and exactly which layer guards it: the kit's
`docs/enforcement-contract.md`.

## Commands a session needs

```sh
# record a session handoff (the handoff skill drives this)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-event.py new-handoff --help
# apply a handoff to its workstream (the garden skill drives this)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-garden.py --help
# re-render the wiki's projections (log, orientation index)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-render.py log
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-render.py claude-local
# working-tree integrity check
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-doctor.py
```

Generated by `wiki-dock install`; reinstall to refresh. Edit the wiki's
config, not this file.
